<title>EGYPT: Yield dips on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield dips on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.029 percent from 10.059 percent at the previous auction on December 25.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Apr 3, 1997 (Mar 27, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.029 percent (10.059)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 610.900 million (645.575 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 811 million (1.002 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.952-10.048 percent (10.002-10.074)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.952-10.272 percent (10.002-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 110 (83)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 127 (143)</p>
<p>($= 3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
